    "type": "no-defensible-ucr-match",
    "checkedOn": "2026-11-09",
    "reason": "UCR offers courses related to European history, politics, film and literature. These cover topics such as European integration and German Expressionist cinema. They cannot form a curriculum that follows German society, politics and cultural works in depth across several years.",
    "curriculumContext": "The full-time 180 EC curriculum includes linked German language courses, 30 EC of study abroad, 30 EC of electives and a 12 EC thesis.",
    "ucrCourseEvidence": "Two mechanically feasible exploratory plans were tested against the workbook. The first extends modern history with EU politics, law and public economics. The second extends film, literature and cultural analysis. German Expressionism and German or European historical topics contribute real but bounded bridges. Neither plan sustains the target’s regional and cultural inquiry. Language study was evaluated separately, including Dutch, psycholinguistics and stylistics. No unverified elective, external exchange or research project was assumed.",
    "candidateAssessment": [
      {
        "concept": "Germany in European history, politics and society",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          17424,
          17426,
          17427,
          17429,
          17430,
          17431,
          17432,
          17433,
          17434,
          17435
        ],
        "assessment": "The revised plan includes war and historical change, comparative institutions, EU politics and law, public economics, migration, propaganda and environmental justice. European integration and German historical episodes give real bridges. The taught curriculum lacks connected study of the German state, political economy, migration and public debates across periods. The law and economics courses offer comparative frameworks without a continuing German application."
      },
      {
        "concept": "German literature, film and cultural identity",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          17425,
          17428
        ],
        "assessment": "Film and Media includes German Expressionism, and Western Art History and documentary provide related European context. World literature, adaptation, stylistics, memoir and gender history support specific methods and themes. The portfolio does not sustain a sequence of German literature, film or cultural criticism and has no documented recurring German-language corpus."
      },
      {
        "concept": "German language, linguistics and academic writing",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          17422,
          17423
        ],
        "assessment": "Psycholinguistics examines processing and acquisition, Style & Meaning studies form and interpretation, and introductory Dutch offers a related West Germanic language. None teaches German reading, grammar, writing or speech, or analyses German and Dutch systematically in contrast. A German language-centred pathway cannot be assembled."
      }
    ],
